              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "Stone bastion wall of <b><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Fort_Christian\" title=\"Category:Fort Christian\">Fort Christian</a></b>  — at Saint Thomas Harbor in <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Charlotte_Amalie\" title=\"Category:Charlotte Amalie\">Charlotte Amalie</a> on <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Saint_Thomas,_United_States_Virgin_Islands\" title=\"Category:Saint Thomas, United States Virgin Islands\">St. Thomas</a>, U.S. Virgin Islands. \n<ul><li>The mid-17th century colonial <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Danish_forts\" title=\"Category:Danish forts\">Danish fort</a> is the oldest structure in the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:United_States_Virgin_Islands\" title=\"Category:United States Virgin Islands\">United States Virgin Islands</a>.</li>\n<li>On the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:National_Register_of_Historic_Places_in_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands\" title=\"Category:National Register of Historic Places in the United States Virgin Islands\">National Register of Historic Places in the United States Virgin Islands</a> since May 5, 1977.</li></ul>",
